## Core Principles Explained

### 1. Data Leakage Prevention

```
❌ WRONG: Fit scaler on all data, then split
scaler.fit(X)  # Learned on test data!
X_scaled = scaler.transform(X)
X_train, X_test = train_test_split(X_scaled)

✅ CORRECT: Split first, fit on train only
X_train, X_test = train_test_split(X)
scaler.fit(X_train)
X_train_scaled = scaler.transform(X_train)
X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)

✅ BEST: Use Pipeline (automatic)
pipeline = Pipeline([('scaler', StandardScaler()), ('model', LogisticRegression())])
pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)
y_pred = pipeline.predict(X_test)  # Scaler learned only from X_train
```

### 2. Estimator, Transformer, Predictor API

```python
# All follow same pattern
class MyEstimator:
    def __init__(self, param1=value1):        # Set hyperparameters
        self.param1 = param1
    
    def fit(self, X, y=None):                  # Learn from data
        self.learned_param_ = compute(X, y)   # Store with underscore
        return self                             # Return self for chaining
    
    def transform(self, X):                    # Apply learned transformation
        return X - self.learned_param_         # [Transformers only]
    
    def predict(self, X):                      # Make predictions
        return decision_function(X)            # [Predictors only]
    
    def get_params(self, deep=True):           # For GridSearchCV
        return {'param1': self.param1}
    
    def set_params(self, **params):            # For GridSearchCV
        for k, v in params.items(): setattr(self, k, v)
        return self
```

### 3. Train/Test Split Strategy

```python
# For classification: Use stratified to preserve class distribution
X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(
    X, y, test_size=0.2, stratify=y, random_state=42
)

# For imbalanced data: Still use stratified
# For time series: Don't shuffle, use TimeSeriesSplit for CV

# Rule: NEVER touch test set during training
# Rule: ALWAYS set random_state for reproducibility
```

