## Decision Trees & Flowcharts

### Feature Selection Decision Tree

```
Do you want to reduce features?
│
├─ YES
│  │
│  ├─ Need to compare many feature subsets?
│  │  │
│  │  ├─ YES (Wrapper Method)
│  │  │  ├─ Forward: Start with 0, add best features → Fast, good
│  │  │  ├─ Backward: Start with all, remove worst → Good, slower
│  │  │  └─ RFE: Train, remove worst, repeat → Good, model-dependent
│  │  │
│  │  └─ NO (Filter Method)
│  │     ├─ Linear relationship? → f_classif, f_regression
│  │     ├─ Non-linear? → mutual_info_classif, chi2
│  │     └─ Speed critical? → VarianceThreshold, SelectKBest
│  │
│  └─ Model-based selection?
│     ├─ Tree-based? → Feature importance (built-in)
│     ├─ Linear model? → L1 regularization (Lasso, LogisticRegression)
│     └─ Any model? → Permutation importance
│
└─ NO → Use all features
```

### Imbalanced Data Solutions Flowchart

```
Does your dataset have class imbalance?
(e.g., 95% negative, 5% positive)
│
├─ NO → Use normal classification approach
│
└─ YES
   │
   ├─ Imbalance ratio < 10:1 (moderate)
   │  ├─ Use stratified split
   │  ├─ Use class_weight='balanced'
   │  └─ Use F1-score as metric
   │
   ├─ Imbalance ratio 10:1 - 100:1 (severe)
   │  ├─ Use stratified split
   │  ├─ Use SMOTE for over-sampling
   │  ├─ Use class_weight='balanced'
   │  └─ Use F1-score or ROC-AUC
   │
   └─ Imbalance ratio > 100:1 (extreme)
      ├─ Use stratified split
      ├─ Use SMOTE + undersampling combo
      ├─ Use custom class weights
      ├─ Use threshold tuning
      └─ Use PR-AUC (better than ROC-AUC)

Recommended combination:
Pipeline([
    ('smote', SMOTE(random_state=42)),
    ('scaler', StandardScaler()),
    ('model', LogisticRegression(class_weight='balanced'))
])
```

