## Cross-Validation Strategies

```python
# Standard K-Fold
from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score
scores = cross_val_score(model, X, y, cv=5)  # Default: 5-fold
print(f"Mean: {scores.mean()}, Std: {scores.std()}")

# For classification: Use Stratified K-Fold (preserves class ratio)
from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold
skf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)
scores = cross_val_score(model, X, y, cv=skf)

# For time series: Use TimeSeriesSplit (no future information leakage)
from sklearn.model_selection import TimeSeriesSplit
ts_split = TimeSeriesSplit(n_splits=5)
scores = cross_val_score(model, X, y, cv=ts_split)

# Rule: Always shuffle random_state for reproducibility
```

