## Common Mistakes & Fixes

| Mistake | Why Bad | Fix |
|---------|---------|-----|
| Using accuracy on imbalanced data | 95% accuracy by predicting all negatives | Use F1, ROC-AUC, or PR-AUC |
| Not shuffling data | May create bias (time ordering, sorting) | Set shuffle=True or use randomized CV |
| Fitting scaler on all data | Data leakage from test set | Always split first, fit on train only |
| Not setting random_state | Results not reproducible | Set random_state in all functions |
| Tuning hyperparameters on test set | Overfitting to test set | Use cross-validation on training data |
| Using wrong metric | Optimizing wrong objective | Choose metric matching business goal |
| Not handling missing values | Model crashes or biased results | Use SimpleImputer or KNNImputer |
| Ignoring class imbalance | Model predicts only majority class | Use stratified split, SMOTE, class weights |

