## When to Use Which Algorithm

```
REGRESSION
├─ Linear relationship: Linear Regression, Ridge, Lasso
├─ Non-linear: PolynomialFeatures + Linear, Decision Trees, Random Forest
├─ Feature interactions: PolynomialFeatures, gradient boosting
└─ Sparse data: Lasso (built-in feature selection)

CLASSIFICATION
├─ Linear separable: Logistic Regression, SVM
├─ Non-linear complex: Random Forest, Gradient Boosting
├─ Probabilistic output needed: Logistic Regression, Naive Bayes
└─ Interpretability critical: Decision Trees, Logistic Regression

CLUSTERING
├─ Spherical clusters: K-Means (fast, simple)
├─ Arbitrary shapes: DBSCAN, Hierarchical Clustering
├─ Soft assignments needed: Gaussian Mixture Models
└─ Finding optimal k: Use elbow method + silhouette score

DIMENSIONALITY REDUCTION
├─ Linear relationships: PCA (variance explanation)
├─ Non-linear: t-SNE (visualization), UMAP (scalable)
└─ Feature interpretation needed: Manual selection, feature importance
```

